        text: "Lakshmibai was born in Varanasi in the year 1828. As a child she learnt horse riding, sword fighting and mallakhamb along with her studies. She married the king of Jhansi and became its queen. When the British refused to accept her adopted son as the heir, she raised the flag of freedom. In the battle of 1858 she fought with a sword in each hand, holding the reins of her horse in her mouth. Though the British army was far larger, she refused to surrender. She died on the battlefield at the young age of thirty. The British general himself praised her courage and called her the bravest soldier of the revolt.",
